      "output": "[\"519748632\", \"783652419\", \"426139875\", \"357986241\", \"264317598\", \"198524367\", \"975863124\", \"832491756\", \"641275983\"]"
    }
  ],
  "signature": {
    "method": "solveSudoku",
    "params": [
      {
        "name": "board",
        "type": "String[]"
      }
    ],
    "returns": "String[]"
  },
  "starter_code": "class Solution {\n    public String[] solveSudoku(String[] board) {\n        // TODO: write your solution here\n        return new String[0];\n    }\n}\n",
  "hints": [
    "Fill one empty cell at a time, and undo when you hit a dead end.",
    "Backtracking: for the next empty cell, try each digit not already in its row, column or box.",
    "def solve():\n    find an empty cell (best: the one with the fewest options)\n    if none: return true\n    for d in options: place d; if solve(): return true; remove d\n    return false",
    "Tracking used digits per row/column/box makes each check O(1). Picking the most constrained cell first prunes the search dramatically."
  ],
  "expected_complexity": {
    "time": "O(9^empty) worst case",
    "space": "O(81)"
  },
